E["subzone:ariden-s-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Ariden's Camp",z="deadwind",s="In Deadwind Pass, Ariden's Camp lies abandoned north of the road from Duskwood to the Swamp of Sorrows. Travelers pass beneath Karazhan's shadow and wonder who pitched a tent there.",h="In Deadwind Pass, Ariden's Camp lies abandoned north of the road from Duskwood to the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Silent Encampment",b="North of the road from Duskwood to the Swamp of Sorrows, weathered cloth and cold ashes mark Ariden's Camp. It may once have been an ordinary stop, long abandoned by living men.\n\nDark sorcery has left its mark across Deadwind Pass. No one knows who named the camp for Ariden or what fortune its owner sought near Karazhan. The pass's lingering horrors have swallowed the answer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Ariden's Camp located?",a="Ariden's Camp lies in Deadwind Pass, just north of the main road from Duskwood in the west to the Swamp of Sorrows in the east. It is not far from Karazhan.",al={"aridens camp location","where is ariden camp","deadwind pass camp"}},{q="Are there any active threats at the camp right now?",a="The camp's clearing is quiet and still. Deadwind ogres, spectral apparitions, and foul winged beasts that roost near Karazhan prowl the pass around it.",al={"is aridens camp dangerous","mobs at aridens camp"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may find the deserted camp unsettling so near Karazhan. Few who linger near Medivh's tower stay long.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see that someone made camp beneath a terrifying spire and never returned for their things. The choice seems either ambitious or foolish."},kw={"ariden","ariden's camp","deadwind pass","duskwood","karazhan","medivh","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:deadwind","subzone:karazhan","topic:medivh","zone:duskwood","zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Ariden's Camp"}}
E["subzone:deadman-s-crossing"] = {t="subzone",n="Deadman's Crossing",z="deadwind",s="At Deadman's Crossing, travelers still follow the packed road beneath a tree hung with the dead. The junction in Deadwind Pass links Duskwood, the Swamp of Sorrows, and the track to Karazhan, carrying travelers across the southern Eastern Kingdoms.",h="At Deadman's Crossing, travelers still follow the packed road beneath a tree hung with the dead.",sec={{t="A Grim Intersection",b="Deadman's Crossing joins the roads through eastern Deadwind Pass. The western road runs toward Duskwood and the eastern road toward the Swamp of Sorrows. South, a track climbs toward Karazhan. At the fork stands a twisted hangman's tree, its branches bearing two rotting corpses.\n\nBattered wooden signs warn travelers to turn back and abandon hope. Hostile beasts and dark sorceries haunt the canyon, yet the packed dirt road through the crossing remains clear. Travelers who keep to it avoid the blighted rocks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does each road lead from Deadman's Crossing?",a="The western road from Deadman's Crossing leads to Duskwood, and the eastern road leads to the Swamp of Sorrows. The winding southern path crosses Deadwind Pass toward Karazhan.",al={"where do roads go","crossing directions","deadmans crossing paths"}},{q="Who are the corpses hanging from the tree?",a="No one knows who the corpses were. Deadwind Pass has claimed countless wanderers, bandits, and refugees over the years. Someone raised the gallows tree as a grim boundary marker to warn travelers away.",al={"hanging bodies","dead bodies on tree","who was hanged"}},{q="Is Deadman's Crossing safe for travelers?",a="The crossing and main east-west road are clear, though vicious vultures, ghosts, and ogres fill the surrounding crags and caves. Couriers and adventurers can pass between Duskwood and the Swamp of Sorrows safely by staying on the dirt path.",al={"is it safe","will i get attacked on the road","danger level"}},{q="What do the signs at the crossing say?",a="One weathered sign reads, “Turn Back!” Another warns, “Abandon hope, all ye who enter here.” Both caution travelers about the valley’s dangers.",al={"crossing signpost","what do signs read","abandon hope sign"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance courier traveling from Darkshire to Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands, you can take the quickest route through Deadman's Crossing. The road is unnerving.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde wanderer traveling west from Stonard toward Duskwood, you pass this grim landmark on the way into the blighted human lands."},kw={"deadman's crossing","deadwind pass","duskwood","gallows","hangman's tree","karazhan","signpost","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:deadwind","zone:duskwood","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:karazhan"},src={"Deadman's Crossing"}}
E["subzone:karazhan"] = {t="subzone",n="Karazhan",z="deadwind",s="In Deadwind Pass, Karazhan's sealed tower stirs with dangerous magic. Once Medivh's home, it rises above a meeting of ley lines that twists time, space, and reality. Restless spirits haunt its halls, and dangers remain within.",h="In Deadwind Pass, Karazhan's sealed tower stirs with dangerous magic.",sec={{t="The Guardian's Spire",b="Karazhan rises from ground shaped like a human skull, above a vast meeting of mystical ley lines. Built long before the First War, it was Medivh's refuge and storehouse for his magical secrets. The Last Guardian of Tirisfal lived in its winding halls with his castellan, Moroes. He welcomed noble guests and gathered arcane books and relics said to surpass even the libraries of the Kirin Tor.\n\nYet these walls witnessed Azeroth's greatest betrayal. Possessed by the demon Sargeras, Medivh secretly arranged the opening of the Dark Portal.",sp=0},{t="A Haunted Threshold",b="Anduin Lothar and Medivh's apprentice, Khadgar, killed the Guardian, and Karazhan's gates were sealed. The tower fell into decay, but its powerful ley lines still twist reality. Ghostly echoes, illusions, and distortions of time ripple across Deadwind Pass.\n\nRumors say an evil presence stirs again inside the quiet fortress. Strange beings are drawn to its silhouette. Among them are the shadowy Dark Riders, who search the surrounding lands for forgotten relics.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built Karazhan?",a="No one knows Karazhan's origins, but the tower is known above all as the home of Medivh, the Last Guardian of Tirisfal. Built long before the First War, it rises in Deadwind Pass on skull shaped ground above a powerful meeting of ley lines.",al={"who made karazhan","karazhan creator","origin of karazhan"}},{q="Who was Medivh, and why did he live here?",a="Medivh, son of Aegwynn, was the Last Guardian of Tirisfal, charged with defending Azeroth from demonic threats. He made Karazhan his home and sanctuary, filling it with arcane knowledge, servants such as Moroes, and lavish gatherings that hid his descent into madness.",al={"who lived in karazhan","medivh lore","the last guardian"}},{q="What happened to Medivh in the tower?",a="Since birth, Medivh had been possessed by the spirit of the Dark Titan Sargeras. Under that influence, he used the tower's magic to contact the warlock Gul'dan and open the Dark Portal. Khadgar, Lord Anduin Lothar, and the half-orc Garona uncovered his treachery. They entered Karazhan and killed the Guardian, ending his corruption.",al={"how did medivh die","medivh death","fall of medivh"}},{q="Can you enter Karazhan right now?",a="No. The tower's main gates and threshold remain sealed and warded against intruders. You can wander the abandoned village, crumbling church, and shadowy cellars beneath the surrounding grounds, but the spire itself is shut tight.",al={"can i go inside karazhan","is karazhan open","entering karazhan"}},{q="Why is the area around Karazhan so corrupted and dead?",a="Karazhan sits above a vast meeting of ley lines, whose raw power twists the region around it. Along with the dark demonic sorcery Medivh unleashed inside, that power withered the surrounding canyon into the desolate wasteland called Deadwind Pass.",al={"why is deadwind pass dead","karazhan curse","why deadwind pass empty"}},{q="Who are the Dark Riders connected to the tower?",a="The Dark Riders are a merciless band of relic hunters who haunt Duskwood and the lands around Deadwind Pass in search of powerful artifacts. Who they are and what binds them to the tower remain a mystery.",al={"what are the dark riders","riders of deadwind pass","karazhan riders"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see Karazhan as a monument to the heights and perils of mortal sorcery. Its unmatched collection of artifacts and writings was kept from the Kirin Tor, while unstable ley lines threaten to consume any careless practitioner.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Karazhan holds tragic meaning for Stormwind. Medivh lived there; he was a boyhood friend of King Llane Wrynn and Anduin Lothar. His betrayal within those walls unleashed the First War upon humanity."},kw={"aegwynn","dark riders","deadwind pass","guardian","karazhan","khadgar","medivh","moroes","sargeras","tirisfal"},rel={"topic:medivh","zone:deadwind","topic:anduin-lothar","subzone:dark-portal","topic:first-war","topic:sargeras","topic:dark-riders","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Karazhan"}}
E["subzone:master-s-cellar"] = {t="subzone",n="Master's Cellar",z="deadwind",s="Restless dead haunt Master's Cellar beneath the ruined hamlet south of Karazhan. Wine and provisions once filled its vaults for Medivh's estate; now the dead crowd its cellars and caverns.",h="Restless dead haunt Master's Cellar beneath the ruined hamlet south of Karazhan.",sec={{t="Haunted Underbelly of Karazhan",b="South of Karazhan, ruined homes mark the hamlet where Medivh's servants, groundskeepers, and attendants once lived. Two entrances in the ruins lead beneath them into Master's Cellar. One opens into vaulted wine cellars. The other descends through broken stone into natural caverns. Whatever dark fate overtook Karazhan and its master reached the hamlet too. Caretakers, wailing spectres, and damned souls remain trapped below, bound to endless service.",sp=0},{t="The Lower Caverns",b="At the deepest reach of Master's Cellar, the Lower Cellar opens into the rock beneath Deadwind Pass. The floor and foundations crumbled into natural caverns, leaving a jagged maze where ghostly wails travel through the stone. Few living souls enter these depths. Magical corruption from the nearby tower holds the apparitions here, making the caverns perilous, much like the ruins above.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Master's Cellar originally used for?",a="Master's Cellar held wine and provisions for Karazhan. The hamlet above housed Medivh's domestic staff and groundskeepers, who maintained his household and stored supplies and vintage kegs in its vaults.",al={"purpose of masters cellar","what is this cellar","why is there a wine cellar here"}},{q="Why is the cellar full of ghosts?",a="No one knows for certain what befell the hamlet. The dark fate that overtook Karazhan and its master claimed it too. Former servants and villagers now haunt the ruins as restless shades, wailing spectres, and unliving caretakers.",al={"why are there ghosts","who are the undead in the cellar","why is masters cellar haunted"}},{q="How do you access the cave systems below the cellar?",a="Two cellar doorways lie among the ruined buildings south of Karazhan. The eastern entrance opens into the wine cellar; the western one descends through collapsed masonry into the natural caves of the Lower Cellar.",al={"how to get into the lower cellar","masters cellar entrances","where is the cave entrance"}},{q="Is the Master's Cellar directly connected to the interior of Karazhan?",a="No. Master's Cellar lies near Karazhan and once supplied Medivh's estate, but its underground chambers have no open passage into the tower. They remain beneath the village ruins.",al={"does masters cellar lead into karazhan","entrance to karazhan from cellar"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Arcane backlash beneath Medivh's estate left ghostly remnants in the vaults. Ordinary domestic stores now hold lingering spectral energy.",["class:Priest"]="The tormented spectres in the damp vaults are the souls of simple caretakers and servants. The lingering curse on Deadwind Pass denies them peace."},kw={"deadwind pass","karazhan","lower cellar","master's cellar","masters cellar","medivh","unliving caretaker"},rel={"zone:deadwind","subzone:karazhan"},src={"Master's Cellar"}}
E["subzone:morgan-s-plot"] = {t="subzone",n="Morgan's Plot",z="deadwind",s="Restless dead roam Morgan's Plot behind Karazhan in Deadwind Pass. Its ruined chapel and graves hold those who once belonged to Medivh's household.",h="Restless dead roam Morgan's Plot behind Karazhan in Deadwind Pass.",sec={{t="A Grave in the Shadow of the Tower",b="Behind Karazhan, Morgan's Plot lies against rocky slopes. A ruined chapel stands above crypts beneath the earth. Before Deadwind Pass fell into decay, the estate buried those who lived in the tower and on the nearby grounds.\n\nAfter Medivh, the Last Guardian, fell, dark energies seeped into the earth. Restless dead drove away all normal life. Now the unliving wander among the headstones, where servants and figures from Karazhan's history lie buried.",sp=0},{t="Resting Place of Guardians and Servants",b="Medivh was buried at Morgan's Plot after the tragedy that shattered the tower. He was later resurrected before his return during the Third War. The crypts beneath the soil remain a mystery, and old arcane power and unquiet spirits weigh on the graveyard.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Morgan's Plot located?",a="Morgan's Plot lies in southern Deadwind Pass, in a gloomy hollow directly behind Karazhan's high spire.",al={"where is morgans plot","morgans plot location","how to get to morgans plot"}},{q="Who is buried here?",a="Karazhan's household was buried in the graveyard and crypts. After Medivh fell, the Guardian himself was buried here.",al={"who is buried at morgans plot","medivh grave","moroes grave","aegwynn burial"}},{q="What threats can be found at Morgan's Plot?",a="Unliving residents and restless spirits haunt the chapel and grounds, roaming around the gravestones and crypt entrance.",al={"morgans plot mobs","what enemies are here","chapel monsters"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you find defiled graves and roaming unliving at Morgan's Plot. They recall the corrupting taint left where the Guardian's dark fate unfolded.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know Dalaran regards Morgan's Plot with quiet dread. It holds the burial ground of those struck down during Medivh's tragic end."},kw={"crypt","deadwind pass","karazhan","medivh","morgan's plot","morgans plot"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","zone:deadwind","topic:medivh","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Morgan's Plot"}}
E["subzone:vice"] = {t="subzone",n="Vice",z="deadwind",s="Deadwind ogres hold the Vice beside the road to Karazhan. Their camps and earthen mounds mark a bleak, scarred stretch of Deadwind Pass, where travelers face brute strength and dark magic.",h="Deadwind ogres hold the Vice beside the road to Karazhan.",sec={{t="A Desolate Stronghold",b="The Deadwind ogres hold camps across southern Deadwind Pass, beside the road toward Karazhan. Their rough mounds rise among barren earth and jagged rock. Vengeful ghosts and scavenger vultures haunt much of the canyon, yet the ogres defend their camps with fierce violence.\n\nTravelers on the road between Duskwood and the Swamp of Sorrows must cross their territory. No one knows why the clan chose this bleak, magically scarred waste.",sp=0},{t="Brute Force and Dark Arts",b="Deadwind ogres fight with heavy weapons and dangerous arcane magic. Among them, Deadwind warlocks practice crude but lethal fel sorceries among the earthen mounds. Their camps lie close to Karazhan, the abandoned seat of Medivh.\n\nThe road through the canyon is perilous for wandering scholars and solitary scouts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Vice?",a="The Vice is a rugged stretch of southern Deadwind Pass, where rocky ravines and earthen mounds mark the Deadwind ogres’ camps.",al={"the vice deadwind","what is vice","vice area deadwind pass"}},{q="Why are the ogres living here?",a="No one knows why the ogres settled in this inhospitable, haunted gorge. Their warlocks may seek lingering magic from nearby Karazhan, or the clan may use the remote mountain road to prey on travelers.",al={"why ogres in deadwind","deadwind ogre motive","why are ogres at the vice"}},{q="Where does the road through the Vice lead?",a="The road through the Vice winds into the crags of southern Deadwind Pass and leads toward Karazhan, the abandoned tower of the Guardian Medivh.",al={"vice road destination","where does the road go","path through vice"}},{q="What dangers should travelers expect in the Vice?",a="Travelers face aggressive Deadwind ogres who patrol the road and defend their mounds. The clan includes hulking brawlers and warlocks who wield curses and shadow magic.",al={"vice threats","enemies in vice","what attacks you in the vice"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The Deadwind ogres of the Vice wield dark magic. Even an isolated brute clan can tap into corruptive fel energies.",["class:Mage"]="The ogres camp along the direct approach to Karazhan. Their presence raises questions for the Kirin Tor about whether lingering energies from Medivh’s tower influence the local beasts and clans."},kw={"deadwind ogres","deadwind pass","deadwind warlocks","karazhan","ogre mounds","vice"},rel={"zone:deadwind","subzone:karazhan"},src={"Vice"}}
E["topic:dark-riders"] = {t="topic",n="Dark Riders",z="deadwind",s="In Duskwood, the Dark Riders hunt magical relics and terrorize the land. Hooded and merciless, they strike from hiding and leave slaughter behind.",h="In Duskwood, the Dark Riders hunt magical relics and terrorize the land.",sec={{t="Hunters in the Dark",b="Little is known of the Dark Riders' beginnings. Witnesses speak of hooded horsemen with harsh, shrill voices. One was seen using a small gem to receive orders from a master it called only its “Lord.” Across the kingdom, they hunt objects of magical power. Anyone who stands between them and their prize is cut down.",sp=0},{t="Slaughter at the Farmstead",b="The Dark Riders came to Duskwood after strange tremors began radiating from the Scythe of Elune, warping space. The miner Jitters had found the ancient staff inside Roland's Doom, then promptly lost it. The horsemen followed its magical trace to nearby Yorgen Farmstead and demanded the artifact from Sven Yorgen's family. The terrified settlers had no answers. The Riders butchered Sven's wife and children, driving Sven into vengeful madness.",sp=1},{t="Shadows over Duskwood",b="Whispers in Duskwood link the Dark Riders' sinister hunts to the rogue necromancer Morbent Fel. No one knows what binds them, or who the “Lord” they answer to may be.",sp=1,bt={"q164.5"}}},faq={{q="Who are the Dark Riders?",a="The Dark Riders are hooded horsemen who hunt objects of magical power. They slaughter anyone who stands in their way, while their origins and the identity of their master remain a mystery.",al={"black riders","what are the dark riders","who are the riders in duskwood"},it="identity"},{q="What did they do to Sven Yorgen's family?",a="The Dark Riders were hunting the Scythe of Elune, unearthed nearby. Sven Yorgen's wife and children knew nothing of the artifact, so the Riders murdered them without mercy.",al={"sven farm massacre","what happened at yorgen farmstead","why did riders kill svens family"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Why are the Dark Riders in Duskwood?",a="The Dark Riders came to Duskwood, drawn by temporal and magical disturbances from the Scythe of Elune. The ancient artifact had been unearthed in Roland's Doom.",al={"why are dark riders in duskwood","dark riders scythe of elune","what are they hunting"},it="why_here"},{q="Are the Dark Riders undead?",a="No one knows whether the Dark Riders are undead. They speak in harsh, shrill voices and strike from hiding, but what lies beneath their hooded cloaks remains a mystery.",al={"are dark riders ghosts","are the dark riders undead","what are dark riders made of"},sp=1},{q="Are they working with Morbent Fel?",a="The Night Watch has noted suspicious dealings between the Dark Riders and the necromancer Morbent Fel in Duskwood. The exact terms of their alliance remain unknown.",al={"morbent fel and dark riders","morbent fel alliance"},sp=1,it="allies",bt={"q164.5"}},{q="Why are the Dark Riders hostile to travelers?",a="The Dark Riders hunt objects of magical power at any cost. Anyone who crosses their path or possesses knowledge of a relic they seek is treated as an obstacle to be interrogated or slaughtered, just as Sven Yorgen's family discovered at their farmstead.",al={"why do dark riders attack","dark riders hostility","are dark riders aggressive"},it="hostile",add="18495474"},{q="What is the history of the Dark Riders?",a="Little is known of their history. They appeared in Duskwood hunting the Scythe of Elune, murdering Sven Yorgen's family when the farmers could not say where it was, and the Night Watch links them to the necromancer Morbent Fel. One was seen taking orders through a small gem from a master it called its 'Lord'.",al={"dark riders origin","where do dark riders come from","how were dark riders created"},it="history",add="c7ab6d4f"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The Dark Riders' ruthless hunt for the Scythe of Elune threatens the balance. The weapon's feral energies can wreak havoc across Duskwood.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Dark Riders strike just beyond Stormwind's borders and slaughter innocent homesteaders like Sven Yorgen's family. The kingdom's frontier has slipped far from its grasp.",["class:Mage"]="Relentless hunters of magical relics, the Dark Riders show how much blood the pursuit of arcane power can cost."},kw={"ariden","black riders","dark riders","deadwind pass","duskwood","jitters","scythe of elune","sven yorgen"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","npc:jitters","quest:95","subzone:ariden-s-camp","quest:1043","quest:55"},src={"Dark Riders"}}
E["zone:deadwind"] = {t="zone",n="Deadwind Pass",z="deadwind",s="A foul wind sweeps Deadwind Pass, where the road runs between Duskwood and the Swamp of Sorrows. Karazhan rises at the heart of the pass, its ruined tower still tainted by Medivh's death. Ogres and ghosts haunt the canyon, and no town offers shelter.",h="A foul wind sweeps Deadwind Pass, where the road runs between Duskwood and the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Canyon of Bones and Howling Wind",b="Deadwind Pass lies between Duskwood and the Swamp of Sorrows. Its ravines cut through pale stone and petrified wood. Once counted as part of the Redridge Mountains, the pass is now a hollow scar. A foul wind tears through the gorge, and sudden lightning under a gray sky makes metal arms dangerous to carry.\n\nTotemic effigies hang from dead branches beside the main road, warning travelers to keep moving. No fertile soil or mineable veins offer reason to stay. No town or flight master can give aid.",sp=0},{t="The Legacy of Karazhan",b="Karazhan dominates Deadwind Pass, built above a powerful meeting of ley lines. The tower was Guardian Medivh's stronghold, where he plotted to open the Dark Portal and bring ruin to Stormwind. During the First War, Lord Anduin Lothar and the young Khadgar led an expedition into the tower after Medivh's madness and possession came to light. They killed him there.\n\nHis death released fel taint across the pass and Duskwood. Karazhan remains an ominous ruin, and its unstable magic still leaks into the land.",sp=0},{t="Deadwind Ogres and Ruined Plots",b="South of the main road, Deadwind ogres hold the territory around the Vice. Clad in foul rags and armed with jagged iron, they ambush anyone who ventures near the southern road. Reports say they serve a hidden master nearby.\n\nFarther south, Morgan's Plot holds the skeletal remains of a hamlet that once served the tower. Ruins above ground and twisting cellars echo with wailing phantoms and restless shades, the dead left by Karazhan's unleashed sorcery.",sp=0},{t="The Scythe and the Dark Riders",b="Cloaked Dark Riders emerge from Deadwind Pass, then return to its shadows. They have recently terrorized Duskwood, killing innocent homesteaders as they hunt for the Scythe of Elune.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is this place so dead and ruined?",a="Karazhan's magic and Medivh's dark sorcery ruined Deadwind Pass. When Medivh was killed in the tower during the First War, fel magic burst through the ravine. It petrified trees, stripped life from the earth, and blighted the sky.",al={"why is deadwind pass dead","what happened to deadwind pass","why are trees dead here"}},{q="Are there any friendly towns, inns, or flight masters here?",a="No friendly towns, inns, or flight masters serve either faction in Deadwind Pass. Alliance travelers rely on Darkshire to the west in Duskwood. Horde travelers set out from Stonard to the east in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"deadwind pass flight path","is there a town in deadwind pass","deadwind pass inn"}},{q="What is Karazhan's place in Deadwind Pass?",a="Karazhan was Guardian Medivh's tower, where he worked to open the Dark Portal. It remains an ominous landmark amid Deadwind Pass's withered trees, unstable magic, and restless dead.",al={"karazhan deadwind pass","medivh's tower","karazhan history"}},{q="Who are the Dark Riders and where did they come from?",a="The Dark Riders are cloaked figures who ride out of Deadwind Pass to hunt powerful relics, including the Scythe of Elune. They have brought terror to nearby Duskwood.",al={"dark riders deadwind","scythe of elune riders"},sp=1},{q="Can I gather herbs or mine ore in Deadwind Pass?",a="Deadwind Pass has no useful herb or ore gathering nodes. Carrion birds and hostile ogres roam its barren ground.",al={"deadwind pass herbs","deadwind mining","deadwind pass resources"}},{q="Who lives in Deadwind Pass today?",a="Deadwind ogres around the Vice, carrion birds, and restless ghosts occupy the pass. A few wandering human scavengers survive on the move without Alliance support.",al={"inhabitants of deadwind pass","who lives in deadwind","deadwind pass mobs"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The ley lines beneath Deadwind Pass converge at Karazhan. Mages regard the nexus with dread, knowing Medivh warped its arcane conduit to breach dimensional barriers.",["class:Warlock"]="Raw demonic energy still clings to the rocks and stone cellars. Medivh's possession and the pass's necromantic history left a lasting stain of fel magic.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind sees Deadwind Pass as a grim scar on its borders. The horrors from Karazhan ended Duskwood's old splendor and still threaten Darkshire down the western road.",["faction:Horde"]="Travelers heading west from Stonard face a hostile bottleneck. Vengeful human spirits and hulking ogres attack anyone entering the gorge."},kw={"dark riders","deadman's crossing","deadwind ogres","deadwind pass","karazhan","medivh","morgan's plot","the last guardian","vice"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","topic:medivh","subzone:morgan-s-plot","subzone:ariden-s-camp","topic:dark-riders","zone:duskwood","zone:swampofsorrows","quest:1043"},src={"Deadwind Pass (Classic)","Deadwind Pass"}}
